680
00:26:02.180 --> 00:26:04.660
We were laughing on the day when we shot that.
我们拍摄那天一直在笑。

681
00:26:04.660 --> 00:26:06.100
It was so fun to do those.
拍那些真的太好玩了。

682
00:26:06.660 --> 00:26:13.280
I feel like I should let you know that the phone tech rep was played by Rob Brownstein.
我觉得我应该告诉你们，那个电话技术代表是罗布·布朗斯坦饰演的。

683
00:26:13.580 --> 00:26:14.980
He looked familiar to me.
我觉得他看着眼熟。

684
00:26:15.160 --> 00:26:16.440
Well, he's been on Monk.
哦，他演过《神探阿蒙》。

685
00:26:16.900 --> 00:26:17.680
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

686
00:26:18.400 --> 00:26:22.500
He was also on the short-lived Law & Order Los Angeles.
他还演过命途多舛的《法律与秩序：洛杉矶》。

687
00:26:22.940 --> 00:26:23.300
Oh.
哦。

688
00:26:23.680 --> 00:26:26.400
He's been on Breaking Bad and on Mad Men.
他演过《绝命毒师》和《广告狂人》。

689
00:26:27.100 --> 00:26:27.760
But, lady.
但是，女士。

690
00:26:28.120 --> 00:26:28.500
What?
什么？

691
00:26:28.800 --> 00:26:30.280
His latest movie.
他最新的电影。

692
00:26:30.540 --> 00:26:30.820
Yeah.
嗯。

693
00:26:31.080 --> 00:26:32.540
Which has not come out yet.
还没上映呢。

694
00:26:32.820 --> 00:26:33.500
Oh, no.
哦，不会吧。

695
00:26:33.700 --> 00:26:34.240
No, wait, wait, wait.
不，等等，等等，等等。

696
00:26:34.260 --> 00:26:34.960
Is it John Wick?
是《疾速追杀》吗？

697
00:26:35.400 --> 00:26:35.920
No.
不是。

698
00:26:36.140 --> 00:26:36.300
Oh.
哦。

699
00:26:37.200 --> 00:26:39.800
It's called Hummingbird.
片名叫《蜂鸟》。

700
00:26:40.080 --> 00:26:40.560
Oh.
哦。

701
00:26:41.380 --> 00:26:42.620
I'll go see it.
我要去看这部电影。

702
00:26:42.760 --> 00:26:44.060
It's a sci-fi movie.
这是一部科幻片。

703
00:26:44.300 --> 00:26:45.200
Listen to the tagline.
听听这宣传语。

704
00:26:45.260 --> 00:26:45.700
I'm in.
算我一个。

705
00:26:45.960 --> 00:26:53.100
When beloved telepathic superhero Hummingbird, also known as Lola Laxman, is left for dead after
当备受爱戴的心灵感应超级英雄蜂鸟，也就是罗拉·拉克曼，在经历了一场大战后

706
00:26:53.100 --> 00:26:57.040
a major battle, she makes a deal with the devil to save her life.
身负重伤奄奄一息时，她为了保命与魔鬼做了交易。

707
00:26:57.380 --> 00:26:58.340
Sign me up.
算我一个。

708
00:26:58.500 --> 00:26:59.380
Sign us both up.
把我们俩都算上。

709
00:26:59.500 --> 00:26:59.800
Yeah.
好啊。

710
00:27:00.360 --> 00:27:01.780
We're going to go see Hummingbird.
我们要去看《蜂鸟》。

711
00:27:01.980 --> 00:27:03.720
I'm going to be in a sci-fi with you.
我要和你一起拍一部科幻片。

712
00:27:04.280 --> 00:27:05.320
Listen, you know what?
听着，你知道吗？

713
00:27:05.380 --> 00:27:11.420
You can be the science lab tech lady that comes in and gives the science behind the thing.
你可以演那个出场解释科学原理的实验室技术员女郎。

714
00:27:11.880 --> 00:27:12.360
Okay.
好的。

715
00:27:12.680 --> 00:27:16.720
You know what I would love to be in is a movie like, what's it called?
你知道我最想演的是哪种电影吗，叫什么来着？

716
00:27:16.800 --> 00:27:17.240
Outbreak.
《极度恐慌》。

717
00:27:18.160 --> 00:27:18.640
No.
不是。

718
00:27:19.420 --> 00:27:19.900
No.
不是。

719
00:27:20.580 --> 00:27:21.540
Not that movie.
不是那部电影。

720
00:27:21.740 --> 00:27:22.580
With Kurt Russell.
库尔特·拉塞尔演的那部。

721
00:27:22.580 --> 00:27:23.480
The Thing.
《怪形》。

722
00:27:24.020 --> 00:27:24.480
Ew.
呃。

723
00:27:24.820 --> 00:27:25.360
The Thing.
《怪形》。

724
00:27:25.700 --> 00:27:26.140
Ew.
呃。

725
00:27:26.360 --> 00:27:26.640
Yeah.
对。

726
00:27:27.040 --> 00:27:27.500
Gross.
真恶心。

727
00:27:27.900 --> 00:27:28.640
Have you seen it?
你看过吗？

728
00:27:28.920 --> 00:27:30.980
I feel like I saw part of it and I had to bail.
我感觉我看了前半部分就看不下去了。

729
00:27:31.140 --> 00:27:31.620
It's so good.
太好看了。

730
00:27:31.720 --> 00:27:33.600
The practical effects in that movie are outstanding.
那部电影里的实体特效太出色了。

731
00:27:34.760 --> 00:27:35.360
All right.
好吧。

732
00:27:35.460 --> 00:27:36.700
Should we get into this episode?
我们要开始聊这集了吗？

733
00:27:36.940 --> 00:27:37.480
We should.
是该开始了。

734
00:27:37.640 --> 00:27:41.680
There is a Valentine's Day blood drive happening, as you guys know.
如大家所知，现在正在举办情人节献血活动。

735
00:27:42.200 --> 00:27:48.560
And I want to point out that the Scranton Business Park went all out with decorations.
我想指出的是，斯克兰顿商业园这次的装饰真是下了血本。

736
00:27:48.960 --> 00:27:49.560
They really did.
确实如此。

737
00:27:49.760 --> 00:27:51.980
I mean, there's a Happy Valentine's Day banner.
我是说，有个情人节快乐的横幅。

738
00:27:51.980 --> 00:27:54.680
There's three red cupids shooting heart arrows.
还有三个拿着心形箭的红色丘比特。

739
00:27:54.960 --> 00:27:58.240
Big hearts with love messages all on the walls.
墙上贴满了写着爱情寄语的大红心。

740
00:27:58.500 --> 00:28:02.340
There's like a vase with like little plastic hearty things on the counter.
柜台上还有一个插着塑料小红心的花瓶。

741
00:28:02.900 --> 00:28:07.160
There's a giant heart on the elevator doors that opens when they get in.
电梯门上甚至有个巨大的红心，电梯一开门就会裂开。

742
00:28:07.160 --> 00:28:10.140
Who is decorating the Scranton Business Park?
到底是谁在给斯克兰顿商业园搞装饰？

743
00:28:10.180 --> 00:28:10.840
I have a theory.
我有个推论。

744
00:28:11.440 --> 00:28:12.300
What's your theory?
你有什么推论？

745
00:28:12.580 --> 00:28:13.680
I think it's Phyllis.
我觉得是菲利丝。

746
00:28:14.340 --> 00:28:16.080
She's married to Bob Vance.
她嫁给了鲍勃·万斯。

747
00:28:16.200 --> 00:28:17.580
He's one of the five families.
他是五大黑帮家族之一。

748
00:28:18.200 --> 00:28:21.800
You might be right, since she can't be the Dunder Mifflin party planner anymore.
你可能说得对，反正她也不能再当邓德米夫林的派对策划了。

749
00:28:22.080 --> 00:28:22.300
Yeah.
是啊。

750
00:28:22.300 --> 00:28:24.820
She's like, Bob, I've got a bin of hearts and cupids.
她大概会说，鲍勃，我这有一箱红心和丘比特装饰呢。

751
00:28:24.820 --> 00:28:26.320
I can put them around the lobby.
我可以把它们放在大堂四周。

752
00:28:26.720 --> 00:28:29.760
I love Phyllis's voice when she's talking to Bob.
我很喜欢菲利丝跟鲍勃说话时的声音。

753
00:28:31.300 --> 00:28:39.120
Well, we also find out that it is Jim and Pam's first and only Valentine's Day as fiancés.
嗯，我们还发现这是吉姆和帕姆作为未婚夫/妻的第一个也是唯一一个情人节。

754
00:28:39.660 --> 00:28:40.000
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

755
00:28:40.000 --> 00:28:46.640
Did you see at two minutes, 41 seconds that Pam's got some real cute dangle pink earrings and a sassy ponytail?
你有没有看到在两分四十一秒的时候，帕姆戴着非常可爱的粉色吊坠耳环，还扎着俏皮的马尾辫？

756
00:28:47.020 --> 00:28:48.600
I love the sassy ponytail.
我好喜欢那个俏皮的马尾辫。

757
00:28:48.840 --> 00:28:49.200
Me too.
我也是。

758
00:28:49.600 --> 00:28:51.260
I do love a sassy ponytail.
我真的很喜欢俏皮的马尾辫。

759
00:28:52.060 --> 00:28:55.060
Kelly has received a Valentine from a secret admirer.
凯莉收到了一份来自神秘爱慕者的情人节礼物。

760
00:28:55.260 --> 00:28:55.600
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

761
00:28:55.780 --> 00:28:56.860
She opens it up.
她把它打开了。

762
00:28:56.960 --> 00:28:59.260
It says, roses are red, violets are blue.
上面写着，红色的玫瑰是红的，紫罗兰是蓝的。

763
00:28:59.560 --> 00:29:03.060
It's time for your dental cleaning and maybe a checkup too.
是时候去做牙齿洁治了，也许还得做个检查。

764
00:29:04.040 --> 00:29:07.240
I want to say that this resonated with me.
我想说这引起了我的共鸣。

765
00:29:08.680 --> 00:29:18.520
I have been Kelly where I've gotten what looks like a personal holiday card and then it's from like my dry cleaner.
我也当过凯莉，收到过看起来像个人节日贺卡的东西，结果其实是我的干洗店发来的。

766
00:29:18.900 --> 00:29:19.420
Yeah.
对啊。

767
00:29:19.600 --> 00:29:20.120
You know what I mean?
你知道我的意思吗？

768
00:29:20.220 --> 00:29:20.540
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

769
00:29:20.800 --> 00:29:25.820
Or a Valentine's Day card that I think, oh, oh, or birthday.
或者是一张情人节卡片，我还心想，哦，哦，或者是生日卡片。

770
00:29:26.280 --> 00:29:27.860
Do you ever get the birthday greetings?
你有没有收到过生日祝福？

771
00:29:28.040 --> 00:29:28.140
Yes.
有啊。

772
00:29:28.240 --> 00:29:31.800
From like, you get like a birthday greeting from your gynecologiSt.
比如，你会收到妇科医生发来的生日祝福。

773
00:29:32.060 --> 00:29:32.360
Right.
对。

774
00:29:32.800 --> 00:29:33.320
Exactly.
没错。

775
00:29:34.400 --> 00:29:38.840
At Christmas, you know, a lot of businesses will send out like a company Christmas card.
圣诞节的时候，你知道的，很多公司都会寄出那种公司圣诞卡。

776
00:29:39.040 --> 00:29:39.200
Yeah.
对啊。

777
00:29:39.500 --> 00:29:42.620
I tape them right up with all my family and friends Christmas cards.
我都直接把它和我的家人朋友的圣诞卡一起粘起来。

778
00:29:43.260 --> 00:29:46.840
It just tickles me to be like, oh, there's like my friend's family.
我就是觉得很好玩，心想，哦，那边是我朋友的家人。

779
00:29:46.960 --> 00:29:47.600
They're so cute.
他们太可爱了。

780
00:29:47.980 --> 00:29:49.160
And there's my aunt and uncle.
还有我姨妈和姨夫。

781
00:29:49.360 --> 00:29:51.240
And there's my air conditioning company.
以及我的空调公司。

782
00:29:51.480 --> 00:29:51.680
Yep.
对呀。

783
00:29:52.000 --> 00:29:55.420
Right there with a little wreath over a giant air conditioning unit.
就在那里，巨大的空调外机上还挂着一个小花环。

784
00:29:55.620 --> 00:29:55.940
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

785
00:29:56.240 --> 00:29:58.580
It goes up on the wall, guys, if you send it to me.
只要你们寄给我，我就把它挂在墙上，伙计们。

786
00:29:58.580 --> 00:30:00.620
This is true about you.
关于你，这确实是真的。

787
00:30:01.680 --> 00:30:07.000
Should we talk about Pam's beautiful Valentine's Day floral arrangement?
我们是不是该聊聊帕姆那盆漂亮的情人节插花？

788
00:30:07.320 --> 00:30:08.160
Oh, we shall.
哦，我们会的。

789
00:30:08.180 --> 00:30:10.700
And I'm putting on my glasses for this conversation.
为了这次谈话，我要戴上眼镜了。

790
00:30:11.020 --> 00:30:11.440
Wow.
哇。

791
00:30:11.740 --> 00:30:12.120
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

792
00:30:12.600 --> 00:30:16.960
At three minutes and three seconds, we get a real nice shot of this flower arrangement
在三分三秒的时候，我们得到了这个插花的特写镜头

793
00:30:16.960 --> 00:30:18.080
that Jim gave Pam.
那是吉姆送给帕姆的。

794
00:30:18.520 --> 00:30:20.760
And now I'm about to be tacky.
现在我要说点俗气的话了。

795
00:30:21.280 --> 00:30:22.580
Oh, okay.
哦，好吧。

796
00:30:22.840 --> 00:30:23.560
Here it is.
就是这个。

797
00:30:23.760 --> 00:30:26.920
I had a friend growing up who worked at our local flower shop.
我小时候有个朋友在当地的花店工作。

798
00:30:26.920 --> 00:30:32.980
She told me that carnations are the cheapest flower, and they use them to fill out arrangements.
她告诉我康乃馨是最便宜的花，他们用它来填充花束。

799
00:30:33.540 --> 00:30:36.060
And another cheap flower they use are daisies.
他们用的另一种便宜的花是雏菊。

800
00:30:36.400 --> 00:30:40.200
So if you want to go cheap, you get carnations and daisies.
所以如果你想省钱，你就会买康乃馨和雏菊。

801
00:30:40.820 --> 00:30:43.880
Jim's Valentine flowers are all carnations and daisies, I'm just saying.
吉姆送的情人节花全都是康乃馨和小雏菊，我只是随口一提。

802
00:30:44.480 --> 00:30:45.880
I noticed it as well.
我也注意到了。

803
00:30:46.020 --> 00:30:46.340
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

804
00:30:46.720 --> 00:30:48.180
So I looked in the script.
所以我去查了剧本。

805
00:30:48.320 --> 00:30:55.340
I wanted to see if there was a script note about Jim's flower arrangement to Pam.
我想看看剧本里有没有关于吉姆送给帕姆的花艺说明。

806
00:30:55.340 --> 00:30:59.780
I want to hear it because I have a theory that I will prove.
我想听听看，因为我有一个理论，而且我会证明它。

807
00:30:59.980 --> 00:31:01.400
I think I can prove it.
我觉得我能证明这一点。

808
00:31:01.660 --> 00:31:01.920
Okay.
好吧。

809
00:31:02.240 --> 00:31:04.140
Here is what the script said.
剧本上是这么写的。

810
00:31:04.360 --> 00:31:05.380
There was a note.
里面确实有个备注。

811
00:31:06.200 --> 00:31:12.020
There is a small bouquet of non-rose flowers on Pam's desk.
帕姆的桌上有一小束非玫瑰的花。

812
00:31:12.360 --> 00:31:12.880
Okay.
好吧。

813
00:31:13.620 --> 00:31:19.640
Well, I think Phil Shea from Props ran with this because later in the episode, when they
我觉得道具组的菲尔·谢伊顺着这个思路做了，因为在这一集的后面，当他们

814
00:31:19.640 --> 00:31:24.820
go to the fancy restaurant with Bob and Phyllis, the same arrangement is on all the tables.
和鲍勃还有菲利斯一起去高档餐厅时，所有的桌子上都摆着同样的插花。

815
00:31:25.340 --> 00:31:25.580
Really?
真的吗？

816
00:31:25.860 --> 00:31:26.240
Yes.
是的。

817
00:31:26.460 --> 00:31:32.380
And if you look up cheap flowers for big events, carnations and daisies, if you have an event,
如果你去查大型活动用的便宜花卉，康乃馨和小雏菊，如果你有什么活动

818
00:31:32.520 --> 00:31:35.540
like a wedding or whatever, they help fill out the arrangements.
比如婚礼什么的，它们能帮把插花撑得更饱满。

819
00:31:35.760 --> 00:31:38.160
So I think Phil was like, okay, great.
所以我觉得菲尔当时的想法是，行，太好了。

820
00:31:38.440 --> 00:31:44.680
I can get this small bouquet of the same arrangement that I'm doing for the dinner at the restaurant.
我可以弄到一小束跟我为餐厅晚宴准备的完全一样的插花。

821
00:31:45.140 --> 00:31:45.500
Yeah.
对。

822
00:31:46.220 --> 00:31:51.040
So in Jim's defense, I don't know, maybe it helped out our props department.
所以为了替吉姆辩护一下，我不知道，也许这帮了我们道具组一个忙。

823
00:31:51.360 --> 00:31:57.040
Well, I'll also have you know, in the same scene at three minutes and 17 seconds, my grocery list is gone.
不过，我也得让你们知道，在同一场戏的第3分17秒，我的购物清单不见了。

824
00:31:57.680 --> 00:32:00.040
So we obviously shot this on a different day.
所以我们显然是在不同的一天拍的。

825
00:32:00.320 --> 00:32:00.680
Yeah.
对。

826
00:32:00.680 --> 00:32:01.800
And I've been shopping now.
而且我现在已经买过东西了。

827
00:32:01.960 --> 00:32:03.900
So in case you were worried, I got all my stuff.
所以如果你们担心的话，我的东西都买齐了。

828
00:32:04.180 --> 00:32:05.580
Michael does not like the flowers.
迈克尔不喜欢这些花。

829
00:32:05.840 --> 00:32:06.020
No.
没错。

830
00:32:06.140 --> 00:32:06.760
He's not a fan.
他不是粉丝。

831
00:32:06.800 --> 00:32:07.720
He puts them on the floor.
他把花放在了地板上。

832
00:32:07.860 --> 00:32:08.100
He puts them on the floor.
他把花放在了地板上。

833
00:32:08.200 --> 00:32:09.140
He doesn't want to see them.
他不想看到它们。

834
00:32:09.340 --> 00:32:10.320
I was like, you know what?
我当时就想，你知道吗？

835
00:32:10.320 --> 00:32:11.840
I get that he doesn't want to see them.
我理解他不想看到这些花。

836
00:32:12.060 --> 00:32:16.040
The floor, couldn't he just like put them like on one of those tables behind her?
但放地上，难道他就不能把花放在她身后那些桌子上吗？

837
00:32:16.160 --> 00:32:16.600
I don't know.
我不知道。

838
00:32:16.680 --> 00:32:17.620
He wouldn't be able to see them.
那样他就看不见它们了。

839
00:32:18.120 --> 00:32:21.300
Well, he goes up to Jim and he says, I need to have a word with you.
好吧，他走到吉姆面前对他说，我有话跟你说。

840
00:32:22.100 --> 00:32:26.240
And he says that today is a very difficult day for many people in the office.
他还说，对办公室里的许多人来说，今天是艰难的一天。

841
00:32:26.700 --> 00:32:32.040
And that Pam and Jim's sexy vibes are creating a hostile work environment.
而且帕姆和吉姆的性感氛围营造了一个充满敌意的工作环境。

