I wondered if she was a real bloodmobile nurse since that was a real bloodmobile.
我很好奇她是不是真的献血车护士，因为那辆献血车是真的。

942
00:37:43.400 --> 00:37:46.820
Yeah, and she seemed kind of no-nonsense, like very comfortable there.
对，而且她看起来雷厉风行，在那里显得非常自在。

943
00:37:47.020 --> 00:37:48.800
Well, she was, in fact, an actress.
嗯，事实上她是一名演员。

944
00:37:49.100 --> 00:37:50.580
Her name is Julie Ramallah.
她的名字叫朱莉·拉马拉。

945
00:37:51.060 --> 00:37:59.340
She has not been on Monk or Law and Order, but she was on several episodes of The Young and the Restless as well as many movies and TV shows.
她虽然没演过《神探阿蒙》或《法律与秩序》，但她出演过好几集的《年轻和躁动不安的人》，还有很多电影和电视剧。

946
00:37:59.340 --> 00:38:02.280
Well, Michael's going to make the mistake of looking at his blood bag.
接下来，迈克尔犯了个错误，去看自己的血袋。

947
00:38:02.600 --> 00:38:03.800
He freaks out a little.
他有点吓坏了。

948
00:38:04.080 --> 00:38:05.660
And he says to her, tell me stories.
他对她说，给我讲讲故事吧。

949
00:38:05.800 --> 00:38:06.160
Say something.
说点什么。

950
00:38:06.360 --> 00:38:06.940
Distract me.
转移我的注意力。

951
00:38:07.460 --> 00:38:08.980
And she says he's cute.
然后她说他很可爱。

952
00:38:09.540 --> 00:38:09.940
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

953
00:38:14.520 --> 00:38:17.320
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

954
00:38:17.320 --> 00:38:18.440
And he passes out.
然后他就晕倒了。

955
00:38:18.960 --> 00:38:19.260
Yes.
是的。

956
00:38:19.480 --> 00:38:20.460
We had a fan question.
我们收到了一个粉丝提问。

957
00:38:20.820 --> 00:38:27.000
Many, many people wanted to know, how do we do these scenes of people giving blood?
很多人、非常多的人想知道，我们是怎么拍摄这些人们献血的场景的？

958
00:38:27.280 --> 00:38:29.920
Some people wanted to know, did they actually give blood?
有些人想知道，他们真的献血了吗？

959
00:38:30.100 --> 00:38:30.560
No.
没有。

960
00:38:30.560 --> 00:38:31.580
Oh, my goodness.
哦，天哪。

961
00:38:31.760 --> 00:38:32.080
No.
没有。

962
00:38:32.540 --> 00:38:32.800
You know.
你知道的。

963
00:38:32.920 --> 00:38:33.760
Not in the episode.
拍摄这一集时没有。

964
00:38:34.100 --> 00:38:37.040
Yes, the next day, but not while we were filming.
对，第二天，但不是在我们拍摄的时候。

965
00:38:37.900 --> 00:38:41.840
The next day with trained professionals and not actors pretending to take blood.
第二天是由专业培训人员操作，而不是演员假装抽血。

966
00:38:41.980 --> 00:38:42.280
Correct.
没错。

967
00:38:42.980 --> 00:38:46.180
I found out how they make fakie blood.
我查到了他们是怎么制作假血的。

968
00:38:46.820 --> 00:38:47.340
Oh.
哦。

969
00:38:47.820 --> 00:38:49.220
Thanks to Randy Cordray.
多亏了兰迪·科德瑞。

970
00:38:49.420 --> 00:38:50.460
How do they do it?
他们是怎么做的？

971
00:38:50.700 --> 00:38:51.100
All right.
好吧。

972
00:38:51.100 --> 00:38:57.680
It's a combination of water, food coloring, and you're not going to believe it.
那是水、食用色素的混合物，而且你绝对猜不到。

973
00:38:58.800 --> 00:38:59.620
One more thing.
还有一样东西。

974
00:39:00.280 --> 00:39:00.820
Wait, wait, wait.
等等，等等，等等。

975
00:39:03.420 --> 00:39:04.320
You'll never guess.
你永远猜不到。

976
00:39:04.520 --> 00:39:05.140
Wait, wait, wait.
等等，等等，等等。

977
00:39:05.160 --> 00:39:06.000
I want to try a guess.
我想猜一下。

978
00:39:06.400 --> 00:39:07.320
You can eat it.
你可以吃它。

979
00:39:07.560 --> 00:39:09.020
I thought you could eat it.
我以为你可以吃它。

980
00:39:09.080 --> 00:39:10.320
I was going to say like Jell-O.
我本想说是像果冻一样。

981
00:39:11.180 --> 00:39:11.860
Nestle's Quick.
雀巢速溶可可粉。

982
00:39:12.640 --> 00:39:13.020
Oh.
哦。

983
00:39:13.540 --> 00:39:13.920
Yeah.
对。

984
00:39:14.480 --> 00:39:16.000
That thickens it a little, I guess.
我想这会让它变浓稠一点吧。

985
00:39:16.080 --> 00:39:16.300
Yeah.
是的。

986
00:39:16.300 --> 00:39:21.420
So our blood was all made by our special effects team led by Ron Nary.
所以我们的血都是由罗恩·纳里领导的特效团队制作的。

987
00:39:21.840 --> 00:39:23.500
Had to make fakie blood that day.
那天不得不制作假血。

988
00:39:23.640 --> 00:39:23.820
Fakie blood.
假血。

989
00:39:24.060 --> 00:39:30.240
Well, I thought the reveal of Hank when Michael comes to was one of the best moments.
嗯，我觉得迈克尔醒来时汉克的出现是最好的时刻之一。

990
00:39:30.460 --> 00:39:31.780
I laughed so hard.
我笑得太厉害了。

991
00:39:31.940 --> 00:39:32.960
It was so perfect.
简直太完美了。

992
00:39:33.140 --> 00:39:33.620
It was so perfect.
简直太完美了。

993
00:39:33.620 --> 00:39:35.240
And then he calls the nurse a waitress.
然后他把护士叫成了服务员。

994
00:39:35.360 --> 00:39:36.660
He's like so out of it.
他当时完全神志不清。

995
00:39:36.860 --> 00:39:38.440
And he finds her glove.
而且他找到了她的手套。

996
00:39:38.680 --> 00:39:39.680
He does.
他是找到了。

997
00:39:39.960 --> 00:39:43.480
And this starts his whole mission to find her.
这就开始了寻找她的整个任务。

998
00:39:43.920 --> 00:39:45.080
To return the glove.
为了归还手套。

999
00:39:45.260 --> 00:39:45.560
Yeah.
对。

1000
00:39:45.560 --> 00:39:47.020
Like Cinderella's slipper.
就像灰姑娘的水晶鞋一样。

1001
00:39:47.180 --> 00:39:47.560
I know.
我知道。

1002
00:39:47.700 --> 00:39:48.460
It's really cute.
真的很可爱。

1003
00:39:49.000 --> 00:39:54.580
We have one more clip from Katie where she just shares her memories of her time on the show.
我们还有凯蒂的一段短片，她在里面分享了自己在节目中的回忆。

1004
00:39:54.720 --> 00:39:57.720
I asked her, anything stick out to you?
我问她，有什么让你印象深刻的事吗？

1005
00:39:57.900 --> 00:40:00.320
And Angela, wait until you hear what she says.
安吉拉，你等着听她怎么说。

1006
00:40:00.460 --> 00:40:01.060
Oh, I can't wait.
哦，我等不及了。

1007
00:40:02.440 --> 00:40:07.900
I don't remember a ton of details about my time on set.
我不记得片场的很多细节了。

1008
00:40:07.900 --> 00:40:15.920
Except for that you guys were on your last day of like a very, very, very long cycle of shooting.
除了你们当时正处在一段非常、非常、非常漫长的拍摄周期的最后一天。

1009
00:40:15.960 --> 00:40:20.240
And everyone was just dead.
每个人都累得要死。

1010
00:40:20.780 --> 00:40:21.580
Tired.
精疲力竭。

1011
00:40:21.580 --> 00:40:24.720
And just ready for a hiatus.
而且都准备好迎接假期了。

1012
00:40:25.140 --> 00:40:28.300
So, um, that is what I remember.
所以，嗯，这就是我记得的。

1013
00:40:28.440 --> 00:40:29.420
But they were lovely.
不过他们人都很好。

1014
00:40:29.800 --> 00:40:31.380
Everyone was great.
每个人都很棒。

1015
00:40:31.820 --> 00:40:40.520
But just like the talk was all about how this hiatus was just so needed.
但大家都在讨论这个假期是多么地必需。

1016
00:40:40.520 --> 00:40:42.140
So, that's what I remember.
所以，这就是我的记忆。

1017
00:40:43.480 --> 00:40:46.580
That and, um, that you guys moved so quickly.
还有就是，嗯，你们动作太快了。

1018
00:40:46.920 --> 00:40:48.260
It was like the fasteSt.
简直快得离谱。

1019
00:40:48.360 --> 00:40:50.520
I don't even know if I got lunch that day.
我甚至不知道那天我有没有吃上午饭。

1020
00:40:50.640 --> 00:40:51.480
Like I showed up.
就像我刚到。

1021
00:40:51.760 --> 00:40:52.860
I did my scene.
拍完了我的戏份。

1022
00:40:52.860 --> 00:40:55.920
And I, I'm pretty sure you guys banged me out.
而且我，我敢肯定你们飞快地就把我打发了。

1023
00:40:55.920 --> 00:40:57.520
And I didn't even get a free lunch.
我甚至连一顿免费午餐都没混到。

1024
00:40:58.380 --> 00:40:59.100
All right.
好吧。

1025
00:40:59.380 --> 00:41:01.940
This was, remember early on?
这事儿，还记得是在早期吗？

1026
00:41:02.260 --> 00:41:07.820
We had to do 18 episodes in a row so that we could create that hiatus for Steve to go
我们不得不连续拍18集，这样才能为史蒂夫腾出假期去

1027
00:41:07.820 --> 00:41:08.360
do a movie.
拍电影。

1028
00:41:08.520 --> 00:41:08.720
Yeah.
对。

1029
00:41:09.100 --> 00:41:10.760
This was that 18th episode.
这就是那第18集。

1030
00:41:11.020 --> 00:41:12.740
We were so wiped.
我们当时累垮了。

1031
00:41:13.180 --> 00:41:13.400
Yep.
没错。

1032
00:41:13.760 --> 00:41:16.260
18 weeks of 12 to 14 hour days.
18周，每天工作12到14个小时。

1033
00:41:16.500 --> 00:41:16.700
Yeah.
对。

1034
00:41:17.160 --> 00:41:22.280
And you guys, you know when you have that stretch of work where you leave work and it's
而且你们，你们懂那种连轴转的工作吗？你下班的时候天已经

1035
00:41:22.280 --> 00:41:25.760
dark out and then you come back to work and it's still dark out.
黑了，然后你来上班时天依然黑着。

1036
00:41:25.920 --> 00:41:26.480
You know what I mean?
你知道我的意思吗？

1037
00:41:26.520 --> 00:41:27.600
Because you're there so early.
因为你来得太早了。

1038
00:41:27.940 --> 00:41:28.160
Yeah.
对。

1039
00:41:28.320 --> 00:41:31.120
And you're just like, and you sort of all look at each other and joke and be like,
然后你们就，大家互相对看一眼，开玩笑说，

1040
00:41:31.660 --> 00:41:32.740
see you in a few hours.
几个小时后见。

1041
00:41:33.100 --> 00:41:34.220
There's a whole thing now.
现在有个新词了。

1042
00:41:34.360 --> 00:41:35.220
It's called clopening.
叫做“闭开班”。

1043
00:41:36.100 --> 00:41:36.500
Clopening?
闭开班？

1044
00:41:36.820 --> 00:41:37.220
Clopening.
闭开班。

1045
00:41:37.460 --> 00:41:42.760
And it's a lot of people who work in the service industry or in the food industry where you have
很多在服务行业或餐饮行业工作的人都有这种经历，你必须

1046
00:41:42.760 --> 00:41:46.440
to close the restaurant and then like a few hours later you have to open it.
打烊关店，然后几个小时后又得开门营业。

1047
00:41:46.580 --> 00:41:46.780
Yeah.
对。

1048
00:41:47.040 --> 00:41:47.440
Clopening.
闭开班。

1049
00:41:47.760 --> 00:41:48.160
Clopening.
闭开班。

1050
00:41:48.360 --> 00:41:49.920
Well, we were in the clopening phase.
好吧，我们当时就处于闭开班的阶段。

1051
00:41:50.020 --> 00:41:50.580
We were.
确实是这样。

1052
00:41:50.760 --> 00:41:55.680
That is hilarious to me because I do remember like when we would wrap after a big stretch like that.
这让我觉得太好笑了，因为我确实记得，每当我们经历那样高强度的一段拍摄杀青时。

1053
00:41:55.920 --> 00:41:57.400
I would get like a cold.
我就会得感冒。

1054
00:41:57.540 --> 00:41:58.160
I would get sick.
我就会生病。

1055
00:41:58.320 --> 00:41:59.240
We talked about that.
我们之前聊过这个。

1056
00:41:59.340 --> 00:41:59.480
Yeah.
对。

1057
00:41:59.660 --> 00:42:02.560
Right now we were about to all get sick.
就在刚才，我们差点全都病倒了。

1058
00:42:02.700 --> 00:42:02.940
Yeah.
对。

1059
00:42:03.140 --> 00:42:03.460
Basically.
基本上是这样。

1060
00:42:03.900 --> 00:42:07.000
And Katie clocked it and has remembered it all these years later.
然后凯蒂注意到了这一点，并且在之后的这么多年里一直记着。

1061
00:42:07.120 --> 00:42:08.300
That's how tired we were.
可见我们当时有多累。

1062
00:42:08.420 --> 00:42:09.360
We were so tired.
我们真的太累了。

1063
00:42:09.760 --> 00:42:11.960
Next up is a scene I'm dying to talk about.
接下来是一场我迫不及待想要聊聊的戏。

1064
00:42:12.160 --> 00:42:13.280
It's in the conference room.
是在会议室里。

1065
00:42:13.940 --> 00:42:17.120
Kelly and Meredith are decorating for the Lonely Hearts party.
凯莉和梅雷迪思正在为“寂寞芳心”派对做装饰。

1066
00:42:17.640 --> 00:42:21.240
Is this a good time to talk about how Meredith is wearing the vest again?
现在是不是该聊聊梅雷迪思又穿着那件背心这事了？

1067
00:42:21.480 --> 00:42:21.920
Yes.
没错。

1068
00:42:22.040 --> 00:42:22.760
The sweater veSt.
毛衣背心。

1069
00:42:22.800 --> 00:42:28.180
It is making its second appearance in the series pretty quickly because it was just in the duel.
它在剧中很快就第二次亮相了，因为它刚才才在决斗那一集出现过。

1070
00:42:28.640 --> 00:42:29.020
Yes.
是的。

1071
00:42:29.140 --> 00:42:33.160
This is the vest that I wore to a press event with John Krasinski.
这就是我当年和约翰·卡拉辛斯基一起去参加媒体活动时穿的那件背心。

1072
00:42:33.620 --> 00:42:36.460
And by the way, it was not Betsy Johnson.
顺便说一句，那不是贝齐·约翰逊的。

1073
00:42:36.700 --> 00:42:37.660
It was Nanette Lepore.
那是娜内特·莱波尔的。

1074
00:42:38.300 --> 00:42:38.860
Fancy.
真高级。

1075
00:42:39.220 --> 00:42:42.840
And Meredith loves it clearly and is wearing it again.
很显然，梅雷迪思对它爱不释手，又把它穿上了。

1076
00:42:42.840 --> 00:42:45.560
They were really, I think, rubbing it in my face.
我觉得他们真的是在故意气我。

1077
00:42:46.580 --> 00:42:48.040
I take it personally.
我这人很记仇的。

1078
00:42:48.160 --> 00:42:48.860
I'm kidding.
我开玩笑的。

1079
00:42:49.140 --> 00:42:53.200
Well, there's something happening now that I, as an actor, am super jealous of.
话说，现在正发生一件事，作为演员的我简直嫉妒得要命。

1080
00:42:53.580 --> 00:42:57.960
Because Jim and Pam are going to go to frickin' lunch with Bob and Phyllis.
因为吉姆和帕姆居然要和鲍勃还有菲莉丝一起去吃该死的午餐。

1081
00:42:58.340 --> 00:43:01.160
Jenna, I would have loved to have been there.
珍娜，我当时也特别想去。

1082
00:43:01.260 --> 00:43:02.740
That looked like so much fun.
看起来太有意思了。

1083
00:43:02.760 --> 00:43:03.880
And I love it.
我太喜欢这个了。

1084
00:43:03.940 --> 00:43:07.960
It's like the thing we talk about when random characters get thrown together.
这就好比我们经常聊的那种情况，当一些八竿子打不着的角色被凑到一起时。

1085
00:43:08.360 --> 00:43:09.360
What's going to happen?
会发生什么呢？

1086
00:43:09.520 --> 00:43:10.340
What's the chemistry?
会有什么化学反应呢？

1087
00:43:10.600 --> 00:43:12.200
I lived for every scene.
我超级期待每一个镜头。

1088
00:43:12.200 --> 00:43:14.680
And there was so much more in the script.
而且剧本里其实有更多内容。

1089
00:43:14.760 --> 00:43:16.680
And there's more in the deleted scenes.
删减片段里还有更多。

1090
00:43:17.480 --> 00:43:19.440
Phyllis and I were so excited for this storyline.
菲莉丝和我对这条故事线兴奋得不得了。

1091
00:43:19.780 --> 00:43:21.460
We're the two St. Louis gals.
我们俩是圣路易斯的姑娘。

1092
00:43:21.720 --> 00:43:22.160
Yeah.
对。

1093
00:43:22.400 --> 00:43:25.060
And we got to have this whole day of shooting together.
我们能有一整天的时间在一起拍戏。

1094
00:43:25.260 --> 00:43:26.420
We got to talk about bowling.
我们还聊了保龄球。

1095
00:43:26.980 --> 00:43:27.500
Yes.
没错。

1096
00:43:28.520 --> 00:43:31.780
We had a fan question from Joe S.
我们收到了一个来自乔·S的粉丝提问。

1097
00:43:31.980 --> 00:43:35.880
Where were the restaurant scenes for the double date filmed?
双人约会的餐厅场景是在哪里拍摄的？

1098
00:43:36.320 --> 00:43:37.420
I will tell you.
我来告诉你们。

1099
00:43:37.420 --> 00:43:42.220
They were filmed at a real restaurant called Barsak Brasier.
它们是在一家名为巴萨克·布拉西尔的真实餐厅拍摄的。

1100
00:43:42.460 --> 00:43:44.920
It was on Lancashire Boulevard in North Hollywood.
它位于北好莱坞的兰开夏大道上。

1101
00:43:45.200 --> 00:43:51.180
We filled the restaurant with background performers who were pretending to be servers and diners.
我们在餐厅里塞满了扮演服务员和食客的群演。

1102
00:43:51.440 --> 00:43:53.400
We had the restaurant for half a day.
我们把这家餐厅包了半天。

1103
00:43:53.640 --> 00:43:56.320
It is no longer in business, but that's where we were.
它已经关门了，但我们当时就是在那里拍的。

1104
00:43:56.320 --> 00:43:58.080
And we ate their real food.
而且我们还吃了他们真正的食物。

1105
00:43:58.240 --> 00:44:03.800
Well, if you look at the tables, there you're going to see Jim's bouquet of flowers to Pam on every table.
如果你看看那些桌子，就会发现每张桌上都摆着吉姆送给帕姆的花束。

1106
00:44:03.800 --> 00:44:05.840
I'll do a side-by-side in our stories.
我会在我们的快拍里放一张对比图。

1107
00:44:06.440 --> 00:44:09.440
And I want to ask you, Jenna, about the scene with the bowling.
我想问你个问题，珍娜，关于保龄球那个场景。

1108
00:44:09.780 --> 00:44:10.060
Okay.
好的。

1109
00:44:10.400 --> 00:44:10.740
All right.
行吧。

1110
00:44:10.900 --> 00:44:14.240
So Bob says, everyone here who's bowled a 280, please raise your hand.
所以鲍勃说，这里所有打过280分的人，请举手。

1111
00:44:14.600 --> 00:44:16.160
And you guys are like super impressed.
然后你们看起来超级崇拜。

1112
00:44:16.460 --> 00:44:16.680
Yeah.
对啊。

1113
00:44:16.680 --> 00:44:18.440
What's the highest bowling number?
保龄球最高能打多少分？

1114
00:44:18.700 --> 00:44:19.100
300.
300分。

1115
00:44:19.560 --> 00:44:20.580
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

1116
00:44:20.800 --> 00:44:21.060
Yeah.
是啊。

1117
00:44:21.060 --> 00:44:21.820
That's a big deal.
那可太厉害了。

1118
00:44:21.960 --> 00:44:23.040
I don't know a lot about bowling.
我对保龄球不太了解。

1119
00:44:23.220 --> 00:44:24.040
I don't know much about bowling.
我对保龄球知之甚少。

1120
00:44:24.300 --> 00:44:26.680
300 is if you get a strike in every frame.
300分就是每一局都全中。

1121
00:44:27.100 --> 00:44:27.540
Wowzers.
哇哦。

1122
00:44:28.220 --> 00:44:28.660
Okay.
好吧。

1123
00:44:28.960 --> 00:44:38.240
Well, there was a whole other storyline where clearly the writers wanted Jim and Pam to be impressed by how cool Bob and Phyllis were.
还有一个完整的故事线，很明显编剧想让吉姆和帕姆对鲍勃和菲莉丝有多酷感到印象深刻。

1124
00:44:38.440 --> 00:44:43.280
There was a whole other scene where you guys talk about how you went to Dave Matthews' band.
还有一个完整的场景，讲的是你们谈论去看戴夫·马修斯乐队的演出。

1125
00:44:43.440 --> 00:44:43.800
Yes.
是的。

1126
00:44:43.960 --> 00:44:45.360
I remember shooting it.
我还记得拍摄情景。

1127
00:44:45.360 --> 00:44:49.700
And they had great seats in that Phyllis like went backstage and all this stuff.
他们在那儿有极好的座位，菲莉丝还去了后台之类的。

1128
00:44:49.900 --> 00:44:50.060
Yeah.
对。

1129
00:44:50.300 --> 00:44:51.320
We're like, oh, my gosh.
我们就觉得，天哪。

1130
00:44:51.500 --> 00:44:52.820
Bob and Phyllis are kind of cool.
鲍勃和菲莉丝还挺酷的。

1131
00:44:54.240 --> 00:44:57.020
And then they excused themselves to the restroom.
然后他们借口去洗手间离开了。

1132
00:44:57.480 --> 00:45:05.000
We got some mail from Emily Y, who really appreciated the callback from Phyllis' wedding about Phyllis being a good bowler.
我们收到了艾米莉·Y的一封邮件，她非常感激菲莉丝婚礼上的那个梗，呼应了菲莉丝是个出色的保龄球手。

1133
00:45:05.340 --> 00:45:05.880
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

1134
00:45:06.020 --> 00:45:07.500
I also enjoyed that.
我也很喜欢那个细节。

1135
00:45:07.500 --> 00:45:13.800
If you guys remember, Bob has a speech at their reception where he refers to Phyllis as, quote, a hell of a bowler.
如果大家还记得的话，鲍勃在他们的婚宴上发表了一段讲话，称菲莉丝为“绝对是个顶尖的保龄球手”。

1136
00:45:13.940 --> 00:45:14.520
That's right.
没错。

1137
00:45:15.040 --> 00:45:18.920
I think we should take a break before we go to Michael's Lonely Hearts party.
我想在我们去迈克尔的“失恋者派对”之前，先休息一下。

1138
00:45:19.480 --> 00:45:20.160
I do, too.
我也这么觉得。

1139
00:45:20.280 --> 00:45:20.820
Is that okay?
这样可以吗？

1140
00:45:21.140 --> 00:45:22.300
I think we should, too.
我觉得我们也应该休息一下。

1141
00:45:22.740 --> 00:45:25.260
Before we go to break, I just want to say one thing.
在休息之前，我只想说一件事。

1142
00:45:25.440 --> 00:45:25.860
What is it?
什么事？

1143
00:45:25.900 --> 00:45:31.940
That I love that Bob says, I don't know how you work with that one jackass and then that new jackass and that other jackass.
我太喜欢鲍勃说的了，我不知道你是怎么和那个混蛋、然后那个新混蛋还有另一个混蛋共事的。

1144
00:45:33.600 --> 00:45:36.500
Yeah, and Phyllis is like, he means Michael, Dwight, and Andy.
对，然后菲莉丝说，他是指迈克尔、德怀特和安迪。

1145
00:45:36.660 --> 00:45:38.340
And Jim's like, oh, I knew who he was talking about.
吉姆就说，哦，我知道他在说谁。

1146
00:45:38.340 --> 00:45:38.640
I knew.
我当然知道。

1147
00:45:40.240 --> 00:45:40.940
All right.
好了。

1148
00:45:41.000 --> 00:45:42.000
Let's go to break.
我们休息一下吧。

1149
00:45:42.240 --> 00:45:52.990
We are back.
我们回来啦。

1150
00:45:52.990 --> 00:46:05.090
And since I shared about my hot feet today, I thought I would also share about another wardrobe malfunction that I discovered during my bathroom break,
既然我今天分享了我的脚底发烫，我想我也顺便分享一下我刚才上厕所时发现的另一个服装事故，

1151
00:46:05.250 --> 00:46:07.810
which is that I put my underwear on inside out today.
那就是我今天内衣穿反了。

