我早该知道你今天的各种趣闻都和《蜂鸟》有关。

1472
00:59:16.710 --> 00:59:19.010
I mean, I couldn't believe it when I was looking her up.
我是说，我查她资料的时候简直不敢相信。

1473
00:59:19.110 --> 00:59:19.970
She played Sienna.
她饰演西耶娜。

1474
00:59:20.370 --> 00:59:23.150
The series was a thriller about a young girl who vanishes.
这部剧是一部惊悚片，讲述一个小女孩失踪的故事。

1475
00:59:24.110 --> 00:59:24.430
Hmm.
嗯。

1476
00:59:24.950 --> 00:59:27.870
The other lady who has entered is Lynn.
另一个登场的女士是琳恩。

1477
00:59:28.250 --> 00:59:28.590
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1478
00:59:28.730 --> 00:59:30.070
She was played by Lisa K.
她由丽莎·K·

1479
00:59:30.250 --> 00:59:30.490
Wyatt.
怀亚特饰演。

1480
00:59:30.770 --> 00:59:32.510
This is her first of four episodes.
这是她四集戏份里的第一集。

1481
00:59:32.850 --> 00:59:33.330
Yes.
是的。

1482
00:59:33.450 --> 00:59:35.550
She's going to become a love interest for Kevin.
她将成为凯文的恋爱对象。

1483
00:59:36.090 --> 00:59:39.590
In addition to her numerous film, television, and commercial credits,
除了她丰富的电影、电视和广告作品，

1484
00:59:39.850 --> 00:59:43.610
such as Donnie Darko, Legally Blonde, and Days of Our Lives,
比如《死亡幻觉》、《律政俏佳人》和《我们的日子》，

1485
00:59:44.110 --> 00:59:45.610
Lisa Wyatt also does stand-up.
丽莎·怀亚特还表演单口喜剧。

1486
00:59:45.610 --> 00:59:50.970
And along with her husband, she coaches other actors in an acting technique,
此外，她和丈夫还在洛杉矶的表演车库，

1487
00:59:52.010 --> 00:59:56.750
acting technique, called The Mechanics of Believability
辅导其他演员一种名为“可信度机制”的表演技巧。

1488
00:59:56.750 --> 00:59:59.090
at the acting garage in Los Angeles.
在洛杉矶的表演车库。

1489
00:59:59.330 --> 01:00:00.630
I thought she was very believable.
我觉得她演得非常可信。

1490
01:00:00.930 --> 01:00:01.610
There you go.
这就对了。

1491
01:00:01.730 --> 01:00:02.390
Spot on.
说得太准了。

1492
01:00:02.550 --> 01:00:05.250
Did you guys all notice that Rhi is dressed like Angela Martin?
大家有没有注意到瑞的穿着像安吉拉·马丁？

1493
01:00:05.550 --> 01:00:05.990
Yes.
是的。

1494
01:00:06.110 --> 01:00:07.250
We got mail about it.
我们收到了关于这事的邮件。

1495
01:00:07.310 --> 01:00:07.490
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1496
01:00:07.490 --> 01:00:09.150
People wanted to know if that was on purpose.
大家想知道这是不是故意的。

1497
01:00:09.890 --> 01:00:11.070
I think so, yes.
我想是的，对。

1498
01:00:11.070 --> 01:00:11.910
Yes, I think so.
是的，我也这么觉得。

1499
01:00:12.010 --> 01:00:12.330
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1500
01:00:12.530 --> 01:00:12.850
Yes.
对。

1501
01:00:13.270 --> 01:00:15.970
Well, Michael's going to bring Lynn right on over to Kevin.
好吧，迈克尔要把琳恩直接带到凯文那边。

1502
01:00:16.170 --> 01:00:17.450
He wants to make a love connection.
他想撮合他们。

1503
01:00:17.850 --> 01:00:19.390
I mean, Michael's playing Cupid.
我是说，迈克尔在扮演爱神丘比特。

1504
01:00:19.650 --> 01:00:20.190
He is.
他确实是。

1505
01:00:20.370 --> 01:00:24.070
Kevin tries to chatter up, but he kind of keeps putting his foot in his mouth.
凯文试图和她聊天，但他有点总说错话。

1506
01:00:24.790 --> 01:00:27.230
He does mention the circle drive-in.
他确实提到了环形汽车影院。

1507
01:00:27.510 --> 01:00:27.930
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1508
01:00:28.070 --> 01:00:28.850
That's a real place.
那是真的有这个地方。

1509
01:00:28.850 --> 01:00:29.490
I looked it up.
我查过了。

1510
01:00:29.550 --> 01:00:31.450
It's in Scranton, and it's still in operation.
它在斯克兰顿，现在还在营业。

1511
01:00:31.890 --> 01:00:35.670
One of my favorites, though, is when Michael tries to set up Meredith.
不过，我最喜欢的桥段之一，是迈克尔试图给梅雷迪思牵线。

1512
01:00:35.970 --> 01:00:36.250
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1513
01:00:36.250 --> 01:00:40.530
He says, so, Eric, you mentioned that you are in tool and dye repair.
他说，埃里克，你提到过你是从事模具维修工作的。

1514
01:00:40.730 --> 01:00:41.630
I loved that.
我太喜欢那个了。

1515
01:00:42.090 --> 01:00:42.190
Yeah.
是啊。

1516
01:00:42.190 --> 01:00:44.090
Do you think he works at Crest Tool and Dye?
你觉得他在Crest模具厂工作吗？

1517
01:00:44.450 --> 01:00:44.910
Probably.
很可能。

1518
01:00:45.230 --> 01:00:46.850
It's on the sign down in the lobby.
大厅的招牌上写着呢。

1519
01:00:46.970 --> 01:00:47.330
Yes.
是的。

1520
01:00:47.550 --> 01:00:49.270
This is like a business park, right?
这就像是个商业园区，对吧？

1521
01:00:49.270 --> 01:00:50.190
Yes, exactly.
是的，完全正确。

1522
01:00:50.630 --> 01:00:51.890
Eric says, I am.
埃里克说，我是。

1523
01:00:52.030 --> 01:00:56.590
And then Michael says, well, Meredith recently had a total hysterectomy, so that's sort of
然后迈克尔说，好吧，梅雷迪思最近做了子宫全切手术，所以这某种程度上算是一种

1524
01:00:56.590 --> 01:00:57.070
a repair.
维修。

1525
01:00:57.370 --> 01:00:58.030
All right.
好了。

1526
01:00:58.190 --> 01:00:59.470
I'll let you two talk.
我留你们两个聊。

1527
01:01:00.110 --> 01:01:03.110
Would you like a guest star breakdown on Eric?
你想听听关于埃里克的客串演员分析吗？

1528
01:01:03.550 --> 01:01:04.410
I would.
我想听。

1529
01:01:06.250 --> 01:01:10.890
And I found a very interesting crossover connection.
我发现了一个非常有趣的跨界联系。

1530
01:01:11.230 --> 01:01:12.230
I know it.
我知道。

1531
01:01:12.550 --> 01:01:13.410
Tell us, Angela.
安吉拉，快告诉我们。

1532
01:01:14.250 --> 01:01:17.810
Jason and I, when he played Eric, we didn't know each other.
当杰森饰演埃里克时，我和他还不认识。

1533
01:01:18.010 --> 01:01:22.790
But years later, we would both be in the Netflix movie Toll Girl together.
但多年后，我们俩一起参演了网飞电影《收费女孩》。

1534
01:01:23.150 --> 01:01:23.630
Yes.
对的。

1535
01:01:23.870 --> 01:01:24.210
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1536
01:01:24.370 --> 01:01:25.130
So crazy.
太疯狂了。

1537
01:01:25.410 --> 01:01:25.810
I know.
我知道。

1538
01:01:25.930 --> 01:01:27.410
A little mini office reunion.
算是一个微型的《办公室》重聚。

1539
01:01:27.670 --> 01:01:30.230
He played the doctor, the pediatrician.
他演的是那个医生，儿科医生。

1540
01:01:30.350 --> 01:01:34.150
When Steve Zahn, who plays my husband and I, we go to meet with the pediatrician because
当饰演我丈夫的史蒂夫·赞恩和我一起去见儿科医生，因为

1541
01:01:34.150 --> 01:01:38.270
our daughter is so incredibly tall at such a young age, and he played the pediatrician.
我们女儿在这么小的年纪就长得这么高，然后他演了那个儿科医生。

1542
01:01:38.610 --> 01:01:40.030
Should we go to the restaurant?
我们该去餐厅了吗？

1543
01:01:40.270 --> 01:01:44.410
We should because Bob and Phyllis have not come back from the bathroom.
我们该去了，因为鲍勃和菲利斯还没从洗手间回来。

1544
01:01:44.870 --> 01:01:45.350
No.
没有。

1545
01:01:45.630 --> 01:01:47.130
And Jim and Pam are very hungry.
而且吉姆和帕姆非常饿。

1546
01:01:47.410 --> 01:01:48.370
Their food is there.
他们的食物已经上桌了。

1547
01:01:48.490 --> 01:01:49.850
This is getting so awkward.
这变得太尴尬了。

1548
01:01:50.170 --> 01:01:53.290
They're discussing, when are you allowed to eat?
他们在讨论，到底什么时候才可以动筷子？

1549
01:01:54.150 --> 01:01:56.930
And Jim says, did you get hot food?
然后吉姆说，你们点的是热食吗？

1550
01:01:57.070 --> 01:01:58.130
And Pam says, no.
帕姆说，没有。

1551
01:01:58.350 --> 01:01:59.250
She got cold food.
她的饭菜变凉了。

1552
01:01:59.370 --> 01:02:00.910
And he said, then I think you need to wait.
然后他说，那我觉得你需要等一下。

1553
01:02:01.190 --> 01:02:01.590
Right.
对。

1554
01:02:01.690 --> 01:02:02.910
You have to wait for the other people.
你必须等其他人。

1555
01:02:03.330 --> 01:02:05.530
And Pam says, Bob got hot food.
然后帕姆说，鲍勃拿到了热腾腾的饭菜。

1556
01:02:05.830 --> 01:02:07.570
And I think his fries are getting cold.
而且我觉得他的薯条正在变冷。

1557
01:02:07.690 --> 01:02:09.610
And then they start eating his fries.
然后他们开始吃他的薯条。

1558
01:02:10.210 --> 01:02:11.690
And then they eat his steak.
接着他们吃了他的牛排。

1559
01:02:11.930 --> 01:02:12.610
I know.
我知道。

1560
01:02:12.610 --> 01:02:15.490
Did you see how I was really eating the steak?
你看到我刚才吃牛排有多投入了吗？

1561
01:02:15.670 --> 01:02:16.530
Lady, I was starving.
女士，我当时快饿死了。

1562
01:02:16.790 --> 01:02:19.590
I was like so excited to eat the fries and the steak.
我当时兴奋得只想吃薯条和牛排。

1563
01:02:19.730 --> 01:02:20.270
That was real.
那是真的。

1564
01:02:20.430 --> 01:02:21.390
That's my real hunger.
那是我真实的饥饿感。

1565
01:02:21.970 --> 01:02:26.310
I thought it rang pretty true just knowing you the way I know you when you get hungry.
结合我对你的了解，当你饿的时候，我觉得这演得挺真实的。

1566
01:02:26.630 --> 01:02:26.810
Yep.
没错。

1567
01:02:26.910 --> 01:02:29.750
That you would not hesitate to take food off someone else's plate.
你绝对会毫不犹豫地拿走别人盘子里的食物。

1568
01:02:30.090 --> 01:02:32.350
Especially because they hadn't been on that plate yet.
尤其是当那些东西还没被对方碰过的时候。

1569
01:02:32.790 --> 01:02:37.470
When I was a caterer, would you take things and nibble?
我以前当宴会服务员的时候，你会不会顺手拿点东西吃？

1570
01:02:37.470 --> 01:02:43.510
You know, when I was clearing the tables, if there was like a roll or like part of a
你知道的，我收拾桌子的时候，如果有餐包或者

1571
01:02:43.510 --> 01:02:46.270
chicken breast that had clearly not been touched, I would eat it.
明显没被碰过的鸡胸肉，我就会吃掉。

1572
01:02:46.370 --> 01:02:49.090
I mean, I was hungry and I, you know, was a struggling actor.
我是说，我很饿，而且我当时你知道的，是个苦命的演员。

1573
01:02:49.150 --> 01:02:50.230
It was a free meal.
这是一顿免费的饭。

1574
01:02:50.390 --> 01:02:52.990
I would sort of piece it together from everybody's plate.
我会从每个人的盘子里东拼凑西凑出一顿饭。

1575
01:02:53.610 --> 01:02:58.350
Let me tell you something, Angela, because you brought up food and eating for me.
安吉拉，我跟你说件事，因为你刚才提到了食物和吃东西对我来说很重要。

1576
01:02:58.870 --> 01:03:00.190
You know, it's important to me.
你知道的，这对我意义重大。

1577
01:03:01.310 --> 01:03:05.950
And it's so important to me, this idea of like being at a large dinner party.
这对我真的很重要，比如那种出席大型晚宴的想法。

1578
01:03:05.950 --> 01:03:08.410
And people are getting served food.
大家都在上菜。

1579
01:03:08.530 --> 01:03:10.050
And when do you get to eat your food?
那你究竟什么时候才能吃上自己的饭？

1580
01:03:10.350 --> 01:03:12.270
That I actually looked it up once.
为此我甚至特意查过资料。

1581
01:03:12.510 --> 01:03:13.750
Like the etiquette of it?
就像礼仪方面的东西？

1582
01:03:13.870 --> 01:03:14.250
Yes.
是的。

1583
01:03:14.710 --> 01:03:22.390
And I read that in a large dinner party, if they're serving something cold, you have to
我看到在一场大型晚宴上，如果上的是冷盘，你必须

1584
01:03:22.390 --> 01:03:28.430
wait for everybody to get their cold dish, like a salad or a cold soup, before you start
等所有人都拿到冷盘，比如沙拉或冷汤，然后才能开始

1585
01:03:28.430 --> 01:03:28.710
eating.
动筷子。

1586
01:03:28.710 --> 01:03:35.130
But if something hot is being served, after two or more people have been served that hot
但如果上的是热菜，在两名或更多人拿到这道热菜

1587
01:03:35.130 --> 01:03:39.470
dish, you can begin eating while you wait for the rest of the party to get their dish.
之后，你就可以在其他人还没上齐菜的时候先吃起来了。

1588
01:03:39.650 --> 01:03:44.810
And I've stuck with that in my life when I've been at like, let's say a table of 10.
在我的生活中，当我坐在比如说十个人的大桌子旁时，我一直遵循这个原则。

1589
01:03:44.810 --> 01:03:50.410
If I get my hot dish, I'm the fourth person to get it, I start eating it because that's
如果我拿到了热菜，我是第四个拿到的，我就开始吃，因为

1590
01:03:50.410 --> 01:03:52.770
what the book said and because I want to.
书上就是这么说的，而且我也想吃。

1591
01:03:53.470 --> 01:03:58.410
But I digged a little deeper since we're on the topic of dining etiquette.
既然我们聊到了餐饮礼仪，我还深入了解了一下。

1592
01:03:58.510 --> 01:03:58.710
Okay.
好吧。

1593
01:03:58.970 --> 01:04:01.890
Here are some other dining etiquette rules for you.
这里还有一些其他的餐饮礼仪规则送给你。

1594
01:04:02.950 --> 01:04:09.810
Apparently, if you get a dinner roll, etiquette says you should only butter one bite at a time.
显然，如果你拿到了一个小餐包，礼仪规定你一次只能在一小口上抹黄油。

1595
01:04:10.010 --> 01:04:11.850
You shouldn't butter your whole piece of bread.
你不应该把整块面包都抹上黄油。

1596
01:04:12.010 --> 01:04:12.710
Get out.
少来这套。

1597
01:04:12.710 --> 01:04:13.590
Isn't that crazy?
是不是很疯狂？

1598
01:04:13.830 --> 01:04:15.630
I'm going to put butter all over it.
我偏要把上面全抹满黄油。

1599
01:04:15.690 --> 01:04:17.050
I butter the whole thing.
我整块都要抹黄油。

1600
01:04:17.230 --> 01:04:18.350
I want more butter.
我要更多的黄油。

1601
01:04:18.850 --> 01:04:21.710
But if you butter it one bite at a time, you might get...
但如果你是一口吃一口地抹黄油，你可能会得到……

1602
01:04:21.710 --> 01:04:22.370
You're double dipping!
你在二次蘸酱！

1603
01:04:23.030 --> 01:04:23.830
But it...
但它……

1604
01:04:23.830 --> 01:04:26.030
No, because you're using a special knife.
不对，因为你用的是一把特殊的刀。

1605
01:04:26.570 --> 01:04:30.190
And you're putting it on your bread and you're taking a bite and then you're doing that knife
而且你把它抹在面包上，咬了一口，然后你又拿着那把刀

1606
01:04:30.190 --> 01:04:32.390
on that shared communal butter again.
再次放回那个大家共用的黄油里。

1607
01:04:33.250 --> 01:04:34.610
Etiquette, I don't think you're right.
关于礼仪，我觉得你可说得不对。

1608
01:04:34.730 --> 01:04:35.910
Well, that's what it said.
好吧，上面就是这么写的。

1609
01:04:36.050 --> 01:04:36.290
Okay.
好吧。

1610
01:04:36.970 --> 01:04:43.930
Also, out of respect for the chef, you should always try several bites of your food before
另外，出于对主厨的尊重，你应该在往食物里

1611
01:04:43.930 --> 01:04:45.430
adding any salt or pepper.
加任何盐或胡椒之前，先尝几口。

1612
01:04:45.650 --> 01:04:47.330
Well, we always say that to our kids.
对，我们总是对孩子们这么说。

1613
01:04:47.750 --> 01:04:49.590
Like, try it before you salt it, guys.
比如，加盐前先尝尝，各位。

1614
01:04:50.150 --> 01:04:55.050
If someone asks you to pass the salt, do you know you're supposed to pass the salt and
如果有人请你递一下盐，你知道你应该把盐和

1615
01:04:55.050 --> 01:04:55.630
pepper together?
胡椒一起递过去吗？

1616
01:04:55.870 --> 01:04:56.330
I do.
我知道。

1617
01:04:56.570 --> 01:04:57.310
They're a pair.
它们是一对。

1618
01:04:57.490 --> 01:04:58.590
They like to travel together.
它们喜欢一起旅行。

1619
01:04:58.850 --> 01:04:59.510
They travel together.
它们一起旅行。

1620
01:05:00.030 --> 01:05:05.750
If you're enjoying a family-style meal, you're supposed to pass the dishes clockwise around
如果你在享用家庭聚餐式的合餐，你应该把盘子按顺时针方向

1621
01:05:05.750 --> 01:05:06.190
the table.
在桌上传递。

1622
01:05:06.290 --> 01:05:06.930
Oh, gosh.
哦，天哪。

1623
01:05:07.030 --> 01:05:08.830
At our family, it's like a free-for-all.
在我们家，简直就像是一盘散沙各凭本事。

1624
01:05:08.970 --> 01:05:09.190
Same.
我也是。

1625
01:05:09.710 --> 01:05:11.950
Also, this one I found very interesting.
还有，我觉得这一条特别有意思。

1626
01:05:12.710 --> 01:05:16.710
If you leave the table and you're in the middle of a meal, do you know where you're supposed
如果你中途离席，也就是在用餐正进行到一半时，你知道你应该

1627
01:05:16.710 --> 01:05:17.690
to put your napkin?
把餐巾放在哪里吗？

1628
01:05:18.510 --> 01:05:19.990
To the left of your plate?
盘子的左边？

